    "result_text": "Full suite green: **277 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented city title-casing with existing-spelling reuse for owner creation.\n\n**New function \u2014 `NormalizeCity.java`** (in the POST pipeline):\n- Title-cases the city (`\"san francisco\"` \u2192 `\"San Francisco\"`), capitalising each word and lower-casing the rest, treating any non-letter as a word boundary (so hyphenated names work too).\n- Before that, checks all existing owners; if any lives in the same city (matched case- and whitespace-insensitively via the existing `DuplicateMatching`), it reuses that owner's **exact** spelling instead \u2014 so `\"mcfarland\"` becomes the seeded `\"McFarland\"`, not the plain `\"Mcfarland\"`.\n\n**Wiring** \u2014 `owners.POST.yml`: inserted the `normalizeCity` step between `build` and `rejectDuplicate` (under the same `transaction` governance), so the normalised city flows through the rest of the pipeline, including the customer-code assignment and the response.\n\n**Tests** \u2014 added two integration tests to `OwnerRestControllerV1Tests`:\n- `createOwnerTitleCasesNewCity` \u2014 new city `\"san francisco\"` returns `\"San Francisco\"`.\n- `createOwnerReusesExistingCitySpelling` \u2014 `\"mcfarland\"` returns the existing `\"McFarland\"`, distinguishing reuse from plain title-casing.\n\nThe `city` field is returned by the existing `RespondWithOwnerCreated` responder (via `OwnerMapper`), so no responder change was needed.",
